# Contributor credits

A name in a README is not credit. When someone is added for a script, proofread, UI, or other contribution, update every surface below in the same change. Use the same name and the same one-line description (script stem included when there is one).

| Surface | Where |
|---|---|
| Patcher README | `README.md` Credits → **EngPatcher contributors** |
| Fansite | `../NLPP-EngPatcher-Site/src/pages/credits.astro`, in the matching section (Proofreading, QA, and so on) |
| Workbench screen | `../nlpp-localization-workbench/kit/NLPP_Translate.html` |
| Workbench docs | `../nlpp-localization-workbench/README.md` and `kit/README.md` |

## Workbench screen

`README.md` in the workbench repo does not show on the page translators have open.

For a finished script, add `stem: "Name"` to `REVIEWED_BY` in `kit/NLPP_Translate.html`. That map is what draws:

- the name on the script-list row
- `proofread by Name` next to the route badge
- **Proofread by Name. This script is finished.** under the script buttons

Then bump the Scripts iframe query in `index.html` (`data-src="kit/NLPP_Translate.html?v=..."`) so a reload picks up the kit. The HTML file is large; edit it with a script, not a partial write that can truncate it.

Do not stop after the two workbench READMEs. Those were the miss for Lyud on `a000`.
